If you're asking for hints to identify things, why have you read Maniac's
Guide to Ascension already? You probably won't be needing that for a
while... You'd better read Mikko's Absolute Beginners' Guide.

Anyway, to get back to your question: there are many kinds of notes. The
ones that are frowned upon here by some of most of us are the notes that
describe which potion is which, which scroll is which, etc., to use when
you're affected by amnesia (caused by scroll or mind flayer).

The concept of "making notes" that the original poster (whose name you
removed) was talking about involves noting that you quaffed a potion,
which incomprehensible message you got, and seeing if you notice any
strange effects later.

Next time (in another game or later in the same game), if you get the same
message, see if you get these effects again. If you do, you might realise
what the potion in question actually does.

Remembering which obscure items give which messages is often difficult
enough without notes...

